{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ES36M9G3bg4YTZ8hhJiLs","type":"tool_result","content":"13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\n18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\n21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\n43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b96477a-1d28-46fc-afd9-3835f48dc447","uuid":"d0470340-5803-45c4-9f86-5cb4d265ba0b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:28:43.357Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"13:If the default highlighting doesn't fit your needs, you can define a custom highlighter. The easiest way to do this is to extend the :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` class which applies a style to any text matching a list of regular expressions.\n18:    from rich.highlighter import RegexHighlighter\n21:    class EmailHighlighter(RegexHighlighter):\n43:While :class:`~rich.highlighter.RegexHighlighter` is quite powerful, you can also extend its base class :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter` to implement a custom scheme for highlighting. It contains a single method :class:`~rich.highlighter.Highlighter.highlight` which is passed the :class:`~rich.text.Text` to highlight.","numLines":4,"totalLines":4},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016ES36M9G3bg4YTZ8hhJiLs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
